<section id="about" class="about-section">
  <h2 class="about-heading">About</h2>

  <div class="about-content">
  <p>
    I’m a cybersecurity student at <a href="https://www.bellevuecollege.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="highlight-link">Bellevue College</a> with hands-on experience in security operations, penetration testing, and tool development.
    I’m drawn to work that sits at the edge of offense and defense understanding how attacks work in order to build better defenses.
  </p>

  <p>
    Most recently I worked as a SOC Analyst with <span class="highlight">PISCES International</span>, analyzing real-time events from critical infrastructure organizations and building
    <a href="https://github.com/liamadale/pisces-scripts" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="highlight-link">custom tooling</a> on top of
    <span class="highlight">OpenSearch</span> and <span class="highlight">ElasticSearch</span> to streamline triage workflows.
    Before that, I founded and led the <a href="https://www.bcinfosec.club/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="highlight-link">Bellevue College InfoSec Club</a>,
    running weekly labs on topics like network exploitation and privilege escalation, competing in <span class="highlight">PRCCDC 2026</span>, and producing educational content for our
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@BC-InfoSec" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="highlight-link">YouTube channel</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Outside of work I maintain a personal homelab, build static sites with
    <span class="highlight">Astro</span> and <span class="highlight">Hugo</span>,
    and write small tools in <span class="highlight">Python</span>.
  </p>

  <p>
    In my spare time I’m usually out hiking, camping, or behind a camera lens.
    I also enjoy experimenting with different linux distros, troubleshooting tech for friends and family, or smashing headcrabs in
    <span class="group/halflife inline-flex font-extrabold cursor-pointer"
          onclick="activateHalfLifeTheme()">
      <span class="letter">H</span>
      <span class="letter">a</span>
      <span class="letter">l</span>
      <span class="letter">f</span>
      <span class="letter">-</span>
      <span class="letter">L</span>
      <span class="letter">i</span>
      <span class="letter">f</span>
      <span class="letter">e</span>
    </span>.
  </p>
</div>

